        {
          "path": "_m/c/0/p/y/fort-clatsop-wp/fort-clatsop-national-memorial.jpg",
          "filename": "Fort Clatsop National Memorial, Oregon (8d87445d-2638-4336-91b5-08e0e4fd123a).jpg",
          "caption": "Exterior of the Fort.\nThis site commemorates the 1805-06 winter encampment of the 33-member Lewis and Clark Expedition. A 1955 community-built replica of the explorers' 50'x50' Fort Clatsop is the focus of the park. The fort, historic canoe landing, and spring are nestled in the coastal forests and wetlands of the Coast Range as it merges with the Columbia River Estuary. The Salt Works unit commemorates the expedition's salt-making activities. Salt obtained from seawater was essential to the explorers' winter at Fort Clatsop and their journey back to the United States in 1806.\nKeywords: focl; Forts; Lewis and Clark Expedition (1804-1806); American history; Discovery and exploration of the Americas; United States -- History -- 19th century",
          "alt": "Exterior of the Fort.\nThis site commemorates the 1805-06 winter encampment of the 33-member Lewis and Clark Expedition. A 1955 community-built replica of the explorers' 50'x50' Fort Clatsop is the focus of the park. The fort, historic canoe landing, and spring are nestled in the coastal forests and wetlands of the Coast Range as it merges with the Columbia River Estuary. The Salt Works unit commemorates the expedition's salt-making activities. Salt obtained from seawater was essential to the explorers' winter at Fort Clatsop and their journey back to the United States in 1806.\nKeywords: focl; Forts; Lewis and Clark Expedition (1804-1806); American history; Discovery and exploration of the Americas; United States -- History -- 19th century",
          "width": 3072,
          "height": 2048,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "NPS staff",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Clatsop_National_Memorial,_Oregon_(8d87445d-2638-4336-91b5-08e0e4fd123a).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
